WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.970
Ginza, Tokyo, 1 January 2026.

2
00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:10.050
One square metre of commercial
land is valued at 67.1 million yen.

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.690
It is Japan's highest
commercial land value,

4
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.470
up 10.9 per cent in a year.

5
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:22.210
In Ome, also in Tokyo, housing land
averages 98,600 yen per square metre.

6
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.730
Same metropolis.

7
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:24.990
So why the gap?

8
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.910
Does Ginza have better soil?

9
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.690
Does the government set the prices?

10
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.370
In this mission, you'll
find out where shops,

11
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:36.110
offices and factories locate, and
test four classic models of the city.

12
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.710
Then you'll see how Singapore uses
public housing to mix its neighbourhoods,

13
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.950
and evaluate the policy.

14
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.760
Your mission: explain why Ginza's
land is worth so much more than Ome's.
